  "description": "HiQPdf Next HTML to PDF Converter for .NET is a core component of the HiQPdf Next Library for .NET, using an advanced, highly accurate and reliable rendering engine that processes modern HTML, CSS and JavaScript content in compliance with the latest standards.\n\nThe converter targets .NET Standard 2.0 and can be used in .NET Core and .NET Framework applications deployed on Windows and Linux platforms, including Azure App Service, Azure Functions and Docker.\n\nThis package includes only the Windows ARM64 runtime. Separate packages are available for Windows x64, Linux or multi-platform runtimes.\n\nCompatibility:\n\n* Windows 11 on ARM64\n* .NET 10.0, 9.0, 8.0, 7.0, 6.0 and .NET Standard 2.0\n* Web, Console and Desktop applications\n\nMain Features:\n\n* Convert HTML with CSS, web fonts and JavaScript to PDF\n* Support modern web standards and technologies\n* Generate PDF/UA and PDF/A compliant documents\n* Add HTML with page numbers in headers, footers and stamps\n* Repeat HTML table headers and footers in PDF pages\n* Control PDF page breaks with CSS in HTML\n* Create outlines and tables of contents from heading tags\n* Convert HTML forms to interactive PDF forms\n* Convert or exclude specific HTML regions\n* Retrieve HTML element positions in the PDF\n* Trigger conversion automatically or manually\n* Render for screen or print media\n* Set PDF security, viewer settings and signatures\n* Set HTTP headers and cookies\n* Use GET and POST requests\n* Convert HTML to images\n* Convert SVG to PDF\n* Asynchronous methods for async/await\n\nDocumentation and code samples:\nhttps://www.hiqpdf.com/hiqpdf-next-html-to-pdf-dotnet",
